  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhile testing the implementation for auto sizes in the latest Chrome betas (v121) I noticed that images using `object-fit: contain` were getting skewed. I've created [a reduced test ](https://codepen.io/joemcgill-the-sasster/full/ZEPemOM)case to demonstrate the behavior I'm seeing.\r\n\r\nI noticed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4654#issuecomment-495266624 that @aFarkas mentioned some known quirks with calculating height with object-fit, so perhaps this is expected behavior? Wondering if @zcorpan has any advice here.",
